908 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 907 0 R
  /Alt (This series of three maps illustrates the progressive filtering steps applied to generate the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) Forest Mask, likely for the High Resolution Layer (HRL) Small Woody Features (SWF) 2021 product. The maps depict an unspecified geographic area with features classified as 'forest' or 'tree cover' shown in orange/red, and 'non-forest' areas in light grey. 1. **Top Map (Initial Thresholding)**: Represents the initial mask derived from applying a 10% canopy cover threshold to the HRL Tree Cover Density (TCD) 2021 product. This stage shows both dense forested areas and numerous small, linear elements in orange/red, which might include features like large hedgerows connected to forests. Fine red lines, possibly representing roads or other linear features, are visible in the grey non-forest areas. 2. **Middle Map (After Morphological Filter)**: Shows the mask after a morphological filter has been applied. This filter removes linear elements from the forest mask that could represent valid Small Woody Features (SWF), ensuring that only dense and compact forested areas remain. Compared to the top map, many fine linear orange features are removed, and the overall orange patches appear more consolidated. The fine red lines previously visible in the grey areas are no longer present. 3. **Bottom Map (After Minimum Mapping Unit Filter)**: Displays the final Forest Mask after a Minimum Mapping Unit (MMU) of 5 hectares (ha) has been applied. This filter removes small forest areas below 5 ha, resulting in only dense and compact forested areas in orange/red. Numerous small, isolated orange patches visible in the middle map are no longer present, demonstrating their removal by the 5 ha MMU criterion. A 10-metre external buffer, also part of the process, would prevent wrongly detected SWF at forest boundaries.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 1584 0 R
>>
endobj

